═══ WHICH MECHANISM ═══
  A (Min60 native) gross R +0.044 ± 0.016

  B: gross R +0.008 ± 0.012   vs A -0.036 ± 0.020   matches A
  E: gross R +0.023 ± 0.014   vs A -0.021 ± 0.022   matches A
  C: gross R +0.003 ± 0.009   vs A -0.041 ± 0.019   DIFFERS from A
  D: gross R -0.007 ± 0.008   vs A -0.051 ± 0.018   DIFFERS from A

  B and E matching A  → physical size, not the timeframe.
  D matching A alone  → the forward horizon in bars.
  neither             → something about the 1-hour bar itself.

  Whatever this suggests needs its own prereg. A mechanism found
  by comparing five arms is a hypothesis, not a finding.
